From ac314b829b326d2d1f8054aaaecf8b8e5e528325 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:03:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Staff headcount, one way into a pool, and a back button
 that goes back
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three of round 4's smaller asks, and one of them is a bug.

**Staff says how big the team is.** The list already showed a total, but it was
the total of the current filter — "3" under the Instrutor chip, with nothing on
screen saying that was three instructors and not three staff. The headcount now
sits beside "Membros" with the roles broken out, and each role is the filter it
describes. The role numbers deliberately do not sum to the total: somebody who
is both admin and instructor is one person and two roles, and the hint says so
rather than leaving it to arithmetic.

**One way into a pool, not two.** The row on Instalações carried both a
clickable name and a "Ver detalhes" link to the same place. The name stays.

**Voltar goes back.** A facility's people counts link into Staff and into the
register, both of which had a fixed back target, so clicking "6 Instrutores" on
a site and then Voltar landed you on the dashboard with no way back to the site
but the browser. Links that cross into another section now carry `?from=`, and
the destination prefers it. `history.back()` is still not the answer, for the
reason back-link.tsx already gives; what was missing was the origin, and the
origin is known when the link is written. `from` is untrusted input and is
validated as a path inside /dashboard — an unchecked back target is an open
redirect, which is what most of back.test.ts is about.

The register gains a back control only when it was linked into, since a
top-level section has no parent to return to otherwise.

