From bfef81ff769aa59a5342945b720e3e5a1d5c54d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:10:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] One density for the sixteen forms that predate the field
 components
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The density pass changed the shared controls in field.tsx and left sixteen
forms untouched, because those forms build their inputs by hand from a local
copy of the old class string. Half the app would have been 36px tall and half
40px, which is worse than either alone.

They now import the classes rather than restating them, so the next change to
the app's density is one edit again. Three cases needed a decision rather than
a swap:

- a const feeding both an `<input>` and a `<textarea>` splits, because a fixed
  height fights `rows`;
- the guardian typeahead's shell keeps `focus-within:`, since a wrapper cannot
  receive `focus-visible:` — it composes the same tokens instead;
- transfer-ownership had no focus outline at all, which reads as an oversight,
  and now has the standard one.

Widths are deliberately untouched here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PaASymUKAx5c46ceXf6GY2
