From 92de13b911c5e3596d4257e1953e69ad0e570b0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:23:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] The dashboard is about you; the licence is about your
 account
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Instalações is the landing page now, which left the dashboard as a second and
worse version of it: the organization's name, its licence, and a count of
facilities and pools that Instalações lists properly one click away.

So the two screens swap what they were carrying. The dashboard answers who am I
signed in as, what am I allowed to do here, and where else is this account open
— and gives one obvious way through to change any of it. Trial state, the
organizations list and transfer of ownership move to "O meu perfil", which is
where somebody looking for their own account details goes looking.

Transfer ownership was on Pessoas, which is a screen about colleagues rather
than about the account. It reads `GET /people`, which is owner-and-admin only,
and the profile page is the one screen everybody can open — so the fetch is
best-effort and an instructor's `forbidden_role` renders the page without the
block rather than an error banner. That is the thing a later refactor would get
wrong, so it says so in a comment.

The facility and pool counts are dropped rather than moved, and the "add your
first site" nudge with them: Instalações has its own empty state and is where
owners and admins land. The operational dashboard the owner wants — metrics and
maintenance — is deliberately absent until there is something real to put in
it, because three counts standing in for it is precisely what this page just
stopped being.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PaASymUKAx5c46ceXf6GY2
